\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\n• Respiratory: Auscultation of the lungs reveals bilateral rales and rhonchi on the right side. No wheezing is appreciated. Diminished breath sounds are appreciated on the right side.\n• Cardiovascular: Auscultation of the heart reveals a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur. Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs are appreciated on the left side. No carotid bruits appreciated.\n• Musculoskeletal: The patient has no joint swelling in the neck. No carotid bruits appreciated. No joint pain or swelling appreciated in the extremities.\n• Extremities: The patient has 1+ non-pitting edema on both lower extremities. No calf tenderness appreciated. No homans sign.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\n• Respiratory: Pneumonia or pulmonary embolism.\n• Diabetes: The patient\'s blood sugars have been running high. We will increase his dose of metformin from 500mg twice a day to 750mg twice a day. We will have his hemoglobin A1c checked today.\n• Hypertension: Hold norvasc for now. Once his respiratory symptoms resolve, we will reassess his blood pressure and adjust his medications as needed.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nThe patient is to go to the emergency department today for a chest x-ray and a CT scan of the chest. He is to hold his norvasc until his respiratory symptoms resolve. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\nCHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nShortness of breath with hemoptysis.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nPatient reports history of diabetes, hypertension, and asthma. He also has a long history of knee pain.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\nPatient reports taking metformin and Norvasc.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fever.\nHENT: Denies bleeding gums.\nRespiratory: Reports shortness of breath, hemoptysis.\nMusculoskeletal: Reports knee pain. Denies lower extremity edema.\nHematologic/Lymphatic: Denies bruising.\n\nVITALS\n\nPulse oxygenation: 94 percent. Blood pressure: 120/70 mm Hg.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nNeck\n- General Exam